# EAS uploads the project to Expo's build servers. That is acceptable only because
# nothing secret travels with it, so the exclusion is stated here explicitly rather
# than inherited from .gitignore and assumed.
#
# The repo root .env holds a Supabase service-role key and production connection
# strings. It is gitignored, and gitignored files are already excluded from the EAS
# upload — this file makes that a stated rule rather than a side effect, because the
# cost of being wrong once is a leaked production credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing in these is needed to build the app.
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/dist
services/api
docs
